{
    "version": "2.7.3",
    "description": "Impactor (formerly PlumeImpactor): sign and sideload IPAs on an iPhone/iPad/Apple TV with an Apple ID, install SideStore or LiveContainer, place pairing files. With the plumesign command-line tool.",
    "homepage": "https://github.com/claration/impactor",
    "license": "MIT",
    "notes": [
        "Impactor talks to the device through Apple Mobile Device Support (usbmuxd). Upstream asks for iTunes;",
        "any of these provides it:",
        "  scoop install -g gesu/Apple-Mobile-Device-Support   (AMDS alone, from an elevated shell)",
        "  iTunes: https://support.apple.com/106372",
        "  Apple Devices app (winget install 9NP83LWLPZ9K): should work too, upstream does not mention it",
        "If Windows sees the iPhone/iPad only as a camera/MTP device, the USB driver is missing:",
        "  scoop install gesu/Apple-Mobile-Drivers-Installer   (then run it as administrator)",
        "",
        "Closing the window keeps Impactor running in the tray (for auto-refresh); quit it from the tray icon",
        "before 'scoop update Impactor'.",
        "",
        "Accounts, certificate keys and the refresh list live in %APPDATA%\\PlumeImpactor and are kept on uninstall.",
        "If you turned on start with Windows, uninstall removes that entry."
    ],
